      "attachment_url": null,
      "attachment_description": null,
      "comments": "These distant peaks had several crowns along convexities and ridgelines. We noticed these avalanches today but the timing is likely withing the last 48 hours. One distinct avalanche pulled out a relatively low angle pocket but it looks like it stepped into older persistent weak snow from possible the 2/13 crust/facets. I can see through binoculars the distinct texture, depth, and discoloration of the old snow. Winds from the west has deposited this dry snow to leeward aspects and crossloaded terrain features making travel through this terrain complex.",
